/*

A JCL job has three main components:

1. JOB Statement - Identifies the job
//JOBNAME  JOB (ACCT),'DESCRIPTION',CLASS=A,MSGCLASS=X

2. EXEC Statement - Executes a program or procedure
//STEPNAME EXEC PGM=PROGNAME

3. DD Statements - Define datasets
//DDNAME   DD DSN=DATASET.NAME,DISP=SHR

Example:
//MYJOB    JOB (ACCT),'MY JOB',CLASS=A,MSGCLASS=X
//STEP1    EXEC PGM=IEFBR14
//DD1      DD DSN=MY.DATASET,DISP=(NEW,CATLG,DELETE),
//            UNIT=SYSDA,SPACE=(TRK,(5,1))

The SPACE parameter allocates disk space:

SPACE=(unit,(primary,secondary,directory))

Units:
- TRK - Tracks
- CYL - Cylinders
- nnn - Block size in bytes

Examples:
//DD1 DD DSN=MY.FILE,DISP=(NEW,CATLG,DELETE),
//       UNIT=SYSDA,SPACE=(TRK,(10,5))

//DD2 DD DSN=MY.PDS,DISP=(NEW,CATLG,DELETE),
//       UNIT=SYSDA,SPACE=(CYL,(5,2,20))

The third value (20) is directory blocks for PDS.

The DCB parameter defines dataset characteristics:

DCB=(RECFM=xx,LRECL=nnn,BLKSIZE=nnn,DSORG=xx)

RECFM (Record Format):
- F - Fixed length
- FB - Fixed blocked
- V - Variable length
- VB - Variable blocked
- U - Undefined

LRECL - Logical record length
BLKSIZE - Block size

DSORG (Dataset Organization):
- PS - Physical sequential
- PO - Partitioned (PDS)

Examples:
//DD1 DD DSN=FB.FILE,DISP=(NEW,CATLG),UNIT=SYSDA,
//       SPACE=(TRK,(10,5)),
//       DCB=(RECFM=FB,LRECL=80,BLKSIZE=8000)

//DD2 DD DSN=VB.FILE,DISP=(NEW,CATLG),UNIT=SYSDA,
//       SPACE=(TRK,(10,5)),
